   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        
                    </ab>
                </div> <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1922-08-29">29th August 1922</date>
                        </dateline> <salute>Dear Miss Weaver</salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>Enclosed mysterious telegram has just arrived. I don’t know if <name type="person" key="hosf72">Dr Hosford</name> means 5, Harley Street at any time on Thursday or five o’clock in the <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">afternoon</seg>. There has been no reply from <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name>.</p>
                    <p>There is no tension this morning but I have to go in the afternoon to <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">the Hospital for leeches</seg> again.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kindest regards,</salute>
                        <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Since Dr John Stroud Hosford was based at 62 Harley Street, London, the “5” in the “mysterious telegram” probably meant 5pm.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">See also the treatment with leeches by Dr Louis Colin, on JJ’s holiday in Nice in the later months of 1922, who applied five leeches to drain blood from his eyes (<name type="work">JJ</name> 538).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
